WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.954
Here's a classical symphony
that should sound hasty,

00:02.954 --> 00:05.851
generated by a model trained
on free-form captions.

00:06.150 --> 00:10.150
[♪ free-form captions (base model)]

00:10.150 --> 00:13.871
With the same prompt, next comes
music generated by our method,

00:13.871 --> 00:16.884
which rewrites the input
into a structured caption.

00:17.183 --> 00:21.183
[♪ ours: structured captions + rewriter]

00:22.983 --> 00:26.745
Free-form captions mention
some details and skip others.

00:27.033 --> 00:30.438
So we fine-tune on structured
captions, or SCAPs:

00:30.438 --> 00:35.857
the same fields every time, from genre
and mood to tempo, key and instruments.

00:37.350 --> 00:41.387
These details might be missing
from user input, so at inference,

00:41.387 --> 00:44.920
we propose a two-step rewriter
that converts the prompt.

00:45.217 --> 00:49.366
It transcribes what you asked
for, then infers the rest:

00:49.366 --> 00:55.294
high energy, 140 beats per minute, C minor,
strings, flute, trumpet and timpani.

00:56.783 --> 01:01.638
How do we evaluate whether generated
music adheres to what the prompt asks?

01:01.638 --> 01:07.464
Here we introduce Music DSG, a Davidsonian
Scene Graph approach that turns evaluation into

01:07.464 --> 01:08.111
decisions:

01:08.111 --> 01:13.548
yes-or-no questions from the prompt, each
answered from the audio with a confidence.

01:13.833 --> 01:16.233
The free-form model fails all three.

01:16.233 --> 01:17.966
Our model passes them all.

01:19.750 --> 01:24.873
We empirically show that Music DSG is more
aligned with human preference than conventional

01:24.873 --> 01:26.809
embedding-based metrics like CLAP.

01:29.700 --> 01:30.815
One more example.

01:31.100 --> 01:34.100
[♪ post-rock, free-form captions]

01:34.100 --> 01:37.100
[♪ post-rock, ours]

01:38.400 --> 01:40.387
On the Song Describer benchmark,

01:40.387 --> 01:44.298
structured captions with the
rewriter improve all four metrics.

01:46.583 --> 01:47.718
Want to hear more?

01:47.718 --> 01:49.230
Check out our demo page.
